															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/christoffel" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6314045); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6314045&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795127" alt="christoffel" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6314045)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/christoffel" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6314045); return false;" >christoffel</a></span> <span class="odate time_1591227611 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Jun 2020 23:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4675570">
									

<p>Don't skip leg day, you're hindering our ascension into psionic superbeings.</p>
<p>The image is a plate from Gray's Anatomy, which is in the public domain. I got it from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gray432_color.png">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gray432_color.png</a>.</p>
<p>This was an absolutely amazing set of containment procedures, and I spent a while grinning at it like a madman before I got started. I hope the description was worthy of it.</p>
<p>Bonus Commentary (dead authors make exquisite corpses; the below is strictly paratextual)</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>The Nietzsche reference is, of course, Zarathustra's discourse addressed to the despisers of the body.</li>
<li>I made minor edits to the containment procedures, mostly to align the jigsaw puzzle pieces between the parts. There was no appropriate MTF that I found, so I went with the obvious name, &quot;Jock Jams&quot;. I think the only spiritual change is that special audio was originally used to force the hapless containment sacrifices to skip leg day, and I made it part of what gives the leg-day skipping of such a small group its efficacy.</li>
<li>The quadriceps femoris, or &quot;quads&quot;, is of course a very real muscle group which you may have an instance of in each of your legs. To my knowledge, all of its functions, including hip flexion, are non-anomalous in real life. This doesn't mean you should skip leg day.</li>
<li>Authors here have, in the past, advanced the idea of SCP-internal journals and referenced the titles of articles within; in my view, these are real scientists and use a preprint server, not journals. The specific scpXiv paper is an easter egg, but not a good one; you'll be disappointed.</li>
<li>The &quot;punchline&quot; is really the footnote that says &quot;Generally referred to as 'parapsychology' [&#8230;]&quot;. Arguably, putting it in a footnote after a few already-technical paragraphs is a terrible idea. On the other hand, I like it.</li>
<li>Agrippa's Gym worked towards the alchemical great work of protein-heavy workout elixirs, naturally. They were very bad at alchemy, so no one cared (including them, really; it was mostly a group bonding thing). They basically stumbled on this lightning rod by chance. They aren't actually good at parakinesiology. They are very good at being a dedicated group of anomalous-active exercise buddies.</li>
<li>Why do the former Department of Parapsychology want to kidnap and enslave these gym weirdos? Remember, these people were deskbound nerds whose world has suddenly been upended. They are in <em>dire</em> need of good personal trainers.</li>
<li>Naturally, the Department of Parakinesiology are careful not to breach containment; they worked out how to align their not-yet-ripped quads to a secondary muscular gestalt under their control. In a grand irony, they did this using actually-competent alchemical broscience, which they worked out in probably a couple weeks. To be fair, they read some good alchemy papers on scpXiv.</li>
<li>Don't skip leg day.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
